@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@*
    The app shell: the routed page, and below it the one band that is not a page.

    This used to be a bare `@Body` — the layout existed only because Router needs
    one — and every screen was therefore the whole window. That is why the version
    control and the Report issue button ended up in Home's header: there was no
    place in this app that outlived a route, so anything window-wide had to be
    smuggled into a page and mounted again on the next one. Now there is a place.

    The wrapper is not decoration. `.shell` owned `height: 100vh` while it was the
    only thing on screen; with a sibling below it the viewport height belongs to
    the column that holds both, and `.shell` takes what is left of it. The reason
    that column uses `height` rather than `min-height` is written on `.app-shell`
    in app.css — an indefinite height there collapses the workspace grid's whole
    overflow discipline.
*@

<div class="app-shell">
    @Body

    @* A line of no height whose bottom edge is the footer's top edge, so the tray
       inside it stacks upward off the band without anyone having to know how tall
       the band is. The alternative — a fixed tray offset by the footer's height —
       would need that height as a number, and the band is content-driven.

       A sibling of the footer rather than a child of it, and that is the whole
       point of it being here: a positioned ancestor of the two fixed Modals
       rendered from inside the footer is exactly what the warning on .app-footer in
       app.css forbids. `position: relative` is safe on this element because nothing
       fixed is inside it.

       The tray itself is the shared library's, resolving the shared channel. This
       is the one place in the app that renders one, which is what keeps the single
       live region .design/accessibility.md asks for a fact rather than a hope. *@
    <div class="app-toast-anchor">
        <ToastTray CssClass="app-toast-tray" TestId="app-toast-tray" />
    </div>

    <AppFooter />
</div>
